  era: "Section 14 \xB7 Delhi Sultanate \xB7 1206 \u2013 1526"
  title: Tughlaq Dynasty
  text: The Tughlaqs, from 1320 to 1414, included Muhammad bin Tughlaq, known for bold but failed experiments such as shifting the capital to Daulatabad and a token currency, and Firoz Shah Tughlaq, who built canals and towns. Timur sacked Delhi in 1398.
